## # PolyMark (A Color Scheme Compatible with PolyOS)

## ## About PolyMark

## PolyMark is a Color Schme and Syntax Highlight Rule compatible with PolyOS.
## PolyMark builds on Markdown. The files using PolyMark should have a '.md' extension.

## ## Setting Up

## ###  1. Download the files
## To make this work, you should have the following settings in order in sublime text:

## **Step 1:** Download the following files from 'https://github.com/INTxK/PolyMark'

## - 'Preferences.sublime-settings': You should import, mirror or incorporate preference from the GitHub/PolyMark repository.
## - 'polymark.sublime-color-scheme': This is the color-scheme file that highlights texts in sublime text editor as per the syntax file.
## - 'polymark.sublime-syntax': This is the syntax rule file that determines which patterns to highlight in the editor text.

## ###  2. Place the files
## Place the downloaded files as per the following instruction

## **Step 2:** Place the files 'Polymark.sublime-color-scheme' and 'polymark.sublime-syntax' under the following path '~\Sublime Text\Packages\User\'.

## ### 3. Configure Sublime Text
## Configure the Sublime Text as per the following instruction:

## **Step 3:** Set the Theme to Material Vim Blackboard.sublime-theme (for Compatibility)
## **Step 4:** Set the Color Scheme to 'polymark'
## **Step 5:** Set the Syntax to 'polymark'

## If you find a bug or want to provide feedback, share them [here](https://github.com/INTxK/PolyMark/issues)

# -----

# BODY
# Beginning of File Extensions
file_extensions:
  - pm  # file extention .md or .pm will enable PolyMark
scope: text.polymark

# Beginning of Contexts
contexts:

  # The prototype context is prepended to all contexts but those setting
  # meta_include_prototype: false
  # Beginning of Prototype
  prototype:
    - include: comments

  # A. Main [Rule]
  main:
    # The main context is the initial starting point of syntax.
    # Include other contexts from here (or specify them directly).

    # A1. Date-time-stamp [Rule]
    - include: date-time-stamp

    # A2. Area/Project [Rule]
    - include: area-slash-project

    # A2a. Allow ligatures [Rule] (->)
    - match: '->'
      scope: keyword.operator.arrow.polymark

    # A3. Bold [Rule] (**content**)
    # Matches the opening ** but ensures the closing ** exists later on the line.
    - match: \*\*
      scope: punctuation.definition.bold.begin.polymark
      push: bold-content

    # A4. Itilic [Rule] (*content*)
    # Matches the opening * but ensures the closing * exists later on the line.
    # Note: If the parser sees **, it will take the BOLD rule first.
    - match: \*
      scope: punctuation.definition.italic.begin.polymark
      push: italic-content

    # A5. Custom Tag [Rule] (<tag> Content </tag>)
    - match: '<[a-z]+>'
      scope: entity.name.tag.polymark
      push: custom-tag-content

    # A6a. General Includes [Rule] (KEYWORDS, STRINGS, etc.)
    - include: keywords
    - include: strings

    # A6b. Filename with Extension [Rule]
    - include: filename-extension

    # A7. Markers [Rule] (+, -) followed by text (Keep this near the end)
    - match: '^([\t ]*)([\-+])(\s*)(.+)$'
      captures:
        2: punctuation.definition.marker.polymark
        4: string.unquoted.marker-content.polymark
      scope: meta.marker-definition.polymark

    # A8. Date Header [Rule] (####-##-##)
    - match: \b\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}\b
      scope: entity.name.section.header.date

    # A9. Duration Range [Rule] (##-##-## -> ##-##-##)
    - match: \b\d{2}-\d{2}-\d{2}\s*->\s*\d{2}-\d{2}-\d{2}\b
      scope: meta.date-range.time.span.custom

  # End of A. Main [Rule]
  # -----

  # Beginning of Stand-Alone Rules

  # E1. Area/Project [Rule] (@Area/@Project)
  area-slash-project:
    # The updated regex now allows parentheses in the Area name
    - match: '(@)([^/\n\r]+)(/)(@)([^/\n\r]+(?:/[^/\n\r]+)*)'
      name: meta.area-project-hierarchy.polymark
      captures:
        1: entity.name.tag.area.polymark        # The '@' before Area
        2: entity.name.area.polymark            # The top-level Area
        3: punctuation.separator.polymark       # The '/' separator
        4: entity.name.tag.project.polymark     # The '@' before Project
        5: entity.name.project.polymark         # The Project/Sub-Areas


  # E2. Markdown-style headings [Rule] (H1 through H6)
    - match: ^\s*(#+)(\s+)(.+)$
      captures:
        1: punctuation.definition.heading.markdown  # The '#' symbols
        2: meta.separator.heading.markdown          # The space after the hashes
        3: entity.name.section.heading.$1.markdown  # The text content. $1 dynamically inserts the number of hashes.
      scope: markup.heading.markdown

  # End of E2


  # E3. Incomplete to-do list items [Rule] (e.g., "- [ ] Task")
    - match: ^([\t ]*)(-)(\s+)(\[ \])(\s+)
      captures:
        1: punctuation.whitespace.leading.list.markdown # The indentation tabs/spaces
        2: punctuation.definition.list.begin.markdown  # The hyphen/bullet
        3: meta.separator.list.markdown                # Space after the hyphen
        4: markup.list.task.incomplete.markdown        # The crucial "[ ]" box
        5: meta.separator.list.markdown                # Space before the task text
      scope: markup.list.unnumbered.task.markdown

  # End of E3


  # E4. Completed to-do list items [Rule] (e.g., "- [x] Task")
    - match: ^([\t ]*)(-)(\s+)(\[x\])(\s+)
      captures:
        1: punctuation.whitespace.leading.list.markdown
        2: punctuation.definition.list.begin.markdown
        3: meta.separator.list.markdown
        4: markup.list.task.complete.markdown         # Key difference here: "complete"
        5: meta.separator.list.markdown
      scope: markup.list.unnumbered.task.markdown

  # End of E4


  # E5. Metadata Definition [Rule] ([InnerString]:)
    - match: '(\[)([^\]]+)(\]:)'
      scope: meta.tag-definition.custom
      captures:
        1: punctuation.definition.tag.begin.custom  # [
        2: string.unquoted.tag-name.custom          # InnerString (The highlighted part)
        3: punctuation.separator.key-value.custom   # ]:

  # End of E5


  # E6. Horizontal rule/document separator [Rule] (---)
    - match: ^---$
      scope: meta.separator.document.custom

  # End of E6


  # E7. Blockquote [Rule] (> String)
    - match: ^\s*(>+)(\s*)(.+)$
      captures:
        1: punctuation.definition.blockquote.begin.markdown # The '>' symbol
        2: meta.separator.blockquote.markdown               # The space after '>'
        3: markup.quote.content.markdown                    # The quoted string content
      scope: markup.quote.markdown
  # End of E7


  # E8. Strings [Rule]
  strings:
    # Strings begin and end with quotes, and use backslashes as an escape
    # character.
    - match: '"'
      scope: punctuation.definition.string.begin.polymark
      push: inside_string

  inside_string:
    - meta_include_prototype: false
    - meta_scope: string.quoted.double.polymark
    - match: '\\.'
      scope: constant.character.escape.polymark
    - match: '"'
      scope: punctuation.definition.string.end.polymark
      pop: true
  # End of E8


  # E9. Comments [Rule] (/// Comment)
  comments:
    - match: '///'
      scope: punctuation.definition.comment.polymark # The '///' characters
      push:
        - meta_scope: comment.line.double-slash.polymark # Scope for the entire comment content line
        - match: '.*' # Match any character (including spaces) until the end of the line
          scope: comment.line.double-slash.content.polymark # Scope for the 'String' content

        # After the content is matched, look for the end of the line
        - match: $\n?
          pop: true

  # End of E9


  # E10. Bold [Rule] (**Bold Item**)
  bold-content:
    - meta_scope: markup.bold.polymark

    # E10.1. Check for the closing delimiter first
    - match: \*\*
      scope: punctuation.definition.bold.end.polymark
      pop: true

    # E10.2. Match everything else character-by-character
    # This is much safer and more performant than (.*?)
    - match: .
      scope: markup.bold.content.polymark

  # End of E10


  # E11. Italics [Rule] (*Italicized Item*)
  italic-content:
    - meta_scope: markup.italic.polymark

    # E11.1. Check for closing delimiter
    - match: \*
      scope: punctuation.definition.italic.end.polymark
      pop: true

    # E11.2. Match character-by-character
    - match: .
      scope: markup.italic.content.polymark

  # End of E11


  # E12. Custom Tagging [Rule] (<tag> Content </tag>)
  custom-tag-content:
    # This meta_scope will apply to the entire block of content inside the tags.
    - meta_scope: meta.custom-tag.content.polymark

    # E12.1. Closing Tag [Rule] (Crucial for exiting the context)
    # This must come first to take precedence over the included rules.
    - match: '(</)([a-z]+)(>)'
      captures:
        # FIX: Ensure </ uses 'end' punctuation scope
        1: punctuation.definition.tag.end.polymark
        2: entity.name.tag.polymark
        3: punctuation.definition.tag.end.polymark
      pop: true

    # E12.2. **Include Main Context**
    # This tells the parser to use all the main Polymark rules (headers, lists, bold, etc.)
    # to highlight the content, allowing multiline content and nested syntax.
    - include: main

  # End of E12


  # E13. Date-time-stamp [Rule] (YYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM-SS)
  date-time-stamp: # Rule for strict datetimestamp format
    - match: '\b\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}-\d{2}-\d{2}-\d{2}\b'
      scope: constant.numeric.timestamp.polymark

  # End of E13


  # E14. Email Address Pattern [Rule] (name@provider.com)
    - match: '(\b[\w\.\-]+)(@)([\w\.\-]+\.\w{2,})'
      name: string.quoted.email.polymark
      captures:
        1: constant.character.user-name.polymark  # username (before @)
        2: punctuation.definition.email.at.polymark  # the @ symbol
        3: constant.character.domain.polymark     # domain (after @)

  # End of E14


  # E15. Status Markers [Rule] ([?], [!])
    - match: '\[\?\]'
      scope: markup.status.ind-question.polymark

    - match: '\[!\]'
      scope: markup.status.ind-alert.polymark

  # End of E15


  # E16. Code Markers [Rule] ($ String)
    - match: '^([\t ]*)(\$)(\s*)(.+)$'
      captures:
        2: punctuation.definition.dollar.polymark
        3: punctuation.separator.dollar.polymark
        4: string.unquoted.dollar-line.polymark
      scope: meta.dollar-line.polymark

  # End of E16

  # E17. Status Markers [Rule] ([/], [!], [?], [-])
    - match: '^([\t ]*)(-)(\s+)(\[\/\])(\s+)'
      captures:
        2: punctuation.definition.marker.polymark
        4: markup.status.in-progress.polymark
        5: meta.separator.list.markdown
      scope: markup.list.unnumbered.task.markdown

    - match: '^([\t ]*)(-)(\s+)(\[!\])(\s+)'
      captures:
        2: punctuation.definition.marker.polymark
        4: markup.status.alert.polymark
        5: meta.separator.list.markdown
      scope: markup.list.unnumbered.task.markdown

    - match: '^([\t ]*)(-)(\s+)(\[\?\])(\s+)'
      captures:
        2: punctuation.definition.marker.polymark
        4: markup.status.question.polymark
        5: meta.separator.list.markdown
      scope: markup.list.unnumbered.task.markdown

    - match: '^([\t ]*)(-)(\s+)(\[\-\])(\s+)(.+)$'
      captures:
        2: punctuation.definition.marker.polymark
        4: markup.status.abandoned.polymark
        5: meta.separator.list.markdown
        6: markup.status.abandoned.content.polymark
      scope: markup.list.unnumbered.task.markdown

  # End of E17

  # E18. Filename with Extension [Rule] (filename.ext)
  filename-extension:
    - match: '([\w][\w\-\.]*)(\.[a-zA-Z]{2,5})(?=\s|$|[^\w])'
      captures:
        1: entity.name.filename.polymark
        2: entity.name.extension.polymark
      scope: meta.filename.polymark

  # End of E18


  # End of Script
  # ---
